 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Routes
+
+- `POST /batches/:id/transfer`: body `{ "to": "fridge", "qty": 1.5 }`.
+  `to` must be an existing location ID; `qty` must be a finite positive
+  number with at most three decimal places, no greater than the batch stock.
+  Returns 200 with the batch holding the moved stock. A whole transfer keeps
+  the batch ID; a partial transfer creates a new batch preserving item, lot,
+  expiry and received date. Transferring to the current location is a no-op.
+  Unknown batches return `unknown_batch` (404), unknown destinations return
+  `unknown_location` (400), and invalid or excessive quantities return
+  `invalid_qty` (400). Failed validation changes no stock or ledger entries.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
